import{_ as a,o as n,c as t,a5 as o}from"./chunks/framework.BfQ7H7Qx.js";const u=JSON.parse('{"title":"Neo4j all-node view — 2026-11-15","description":"","frontmatter":{},"headers":[],"relativePath":"feature/neo4j-all-nodes/spec.md","filePath":"feature/neo4j-all-nodes/spec.md"}'),s={name:"feature/neo4j-all-nodes/spec.md"};function i(r,e,d,l,c,p){return n(),t("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[o('<h1 id="neo4j-all-node-view-—-2026-11-15" tabindex="-1">Neo4j all-node view — 2026-11-15 <a class="header-anchor" href="#neo4j-all-node-view-—-2026-11-15" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Neo4j all-node view — 2026-11-15&quot;">​</a></h1><p>Objective: admin can browse every stored Neo4j node, including disconnected nodes, custom labels, brand-associated nodes and non-standard trend identifiers, without altering existing public-trend views. AC: new All nodes mode in existing Admin Graph; direct real Neo4j read, internal-key protected AI API, Business requireAdmin. No mock fallback or graph mutations. Keep property projection allowlist and text/count bounds. AC: keyset pages by elementId (no 10k offset ceiling), parameterized text search over name/business id/labels, up to 200 nodes/400 edges per page, truthful next/previous/refresh/empty/error/loading states. Edges are those between page nodes; explain cross-page links require expansion. No claim whole DB loaded at once. Node expansion accepts explicit admin all scope; default public scope unchanged. UI: reuse graph workspace/canvas/inspector, preserve brand/theme tokens, show all labels including CrawledPost in All mode. Isolated nodes must remain visible even when zoom changes. Read-only bounds and truncation remain clear. New keys admin.trendGraph.{byTrend,allNodes,allNodesHint,allNodesSearch,allNodesEmpty,allNodesPage,allNodesPageSize} parallel vi/en. Existing loading/errors/buttons reused. Light/dark and keyboard-labelled controls required. Out of scope: global DB cleanup/merge/write/export, production access/deploy, edits to deferred node merge, change to public graph privacy rules, unrelated real-data changes already pending in working tree.</p><h2 id="large-graph-upgrade-—-2026-11-15" tabindex="-1">Large-graph upgrade — 2026-11-15 <a class="header-anchor" href="#large-graph-upgrade-—-2026-11-15" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Large-graph upgrade — 2026-11-15&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Replace page-replacing overview with progressive whole-database exploration. Retain bounded API responses (200 nodes/400 edges per request), but remove the aggregate scene cap of 200. Load nodes and relationships via independent cursors so cross-batch links are not silently lost. Manual load next / load all / pause / resume / reset controls; completion only after both cursors finish. Counts show loaded/visible, never invented database totals. Partial/cancelled/error states retain already-loaded data. Query/schema changes during a scan are not a transactional snapshot; refresh restarts it. Use Canvas2D for overview rendering, with pan/zoom, fit, full-screen, collision-aware labels, dimmed links and selected-node emphasis. Maintain keyboard-accessible loaded-node navigation and inspector; legacy trend SVG mode unchanged. Initial/explicit rearrange places connected components in separate regions and isolated nodes in their own grid. Incremental loads preserve existing coordinates; rearrange is explicit. Visual grouping never merges or writes database nodes. AC: demonstrate more than 200 accumulated nodes, cross-page edges, pause/abort/stale-response protection, no repeated-cursor loop, bounded read queries, preserved default public graph rules. Do not restore deferred merge code or write shared DB data. New vi/en keys added in parallel; existing BrandHub theme maintained.</p><h2 id="overview-interaction-parity" tabindex="-1">Overview interaction parity <a class="header-anchor" href="#overview-interaction-parity" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Overview interaction parity&quot;">​</a></h2><p>All-node Canvas must support dragging individual nodes without panning the scene, preserving manually positioned nodes during progressive loads, releasing positions, double-click expansion, type visibility, neighbor highlighting and relationship labels. Selection/hide works for every all-mode node including the first record. Provide selected-node move buttons (single-pointer and keyboard alternative), existing inspector and Vietnamese/English guidance. Presentation only; no DB writes or merge. Preserve public SVG behavior and large-scene Canvas. Theme uses existing tokens.</p><h2 id="rank-one-seeded-breadth-first-scan" tabindex="-1">Rank-one seeded breadth-first scan <a class="header-anchor" href="#rank-one-seeded-breadth-first-scan" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Rank-one seeded breadth-first scan&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Selecting All automatically starts a resumable whole-DB scan: seed with the highest-score public canonical category=all Trend in the latest persisted daily snapshot (score DESC/id tie-break, same ranking as daily list), display/select this root, then breadth-first hops without total depth/fanout caps. After a connected component is exhausted, seed the next unseen node using the existing full-node keyset scan, including isolated/custom/private nodes (admin only). A text filter scopes both endpoints and the starting trend; if no matching ranked trend exists use the next matching stored node and show truthful fallback text. Empty DB completes without invented root. New vi/en instructions, seed/hop/component progress, existing themes/access controls and pause/error/resume retained. No DB writes, no new production access.</p><p>Completion UX: center the first singleton seed; auto-fit the accumulated scene when scan completes only if the user has not manually moved/zoomed the viewport or moved a node. Show deepest observed hop across components, not reset-to-zero final-component depth.</p><h2 id="post-visibility-and-right-button-pan" tabindex="-1">Post visibility and right-button pan <a class="header-anchor" href="#post-visibility-and-right-button-pan" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Post visibility and right-button pan&quot;">​</a></h2><p>All-mode toolbar provides an explicit Hide post nodes switch (CrawledPost), default off. Hiding is presentation-only, retains loaded records and traversal through posts, removes incident rendered links and supports restore via switch/type legend. Mouse right drag pans the whole scene even when starting on a node; left click selects and left drag moves an individual node, left background drag does not pan. Suppress native context menu only on Canvas. Touch background pan and keyboard controls retained. Add vi/en switch label and update interaction hint; existing tokens/light/dark. Public SVG unchanged.</p><h2 id="selection-keeps-relationship-context" tabindex="-1">Selection keeps relationship context <a class="header-anchor" href="#selection-keeps-relationship-context" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Selection keeps relationship context&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Selecting a node highlights its incident relationships (brand accent and thicker line), while all other loaded relationships remain drawn at lower opacity and remain selectable. The focus-links toggle controls emphasis, never removes relationships. Existing explicit node/type hiding still filters incident edges. vi/en toggle label describes highlighting.</p>',13)])])}const g=a(s,[["render",i]]);export{u as __pageData,g as default};
